                <pb facs="0226" n="120" xml:id="pg120"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan informs Mr. Blaine that the good offices of the United States, Brazil,
                    and France have been most cordially accepted by the Government of Chile and the
                    revolutionists, those of England and Germany having been declined.</p>
            </div>
